WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.293
This signal looks valid.

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:04.511
It points to the wrong change.

00:00:04.511 --> 00:00:07.879
Would your review process catch it
before someone acts?

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.685
PolicyWatcher published a change about
Google Gemini Apps

00:00:13.685 --> 00:00:15.902
for work and school accounts.

00:00:15.902 --> 00:00:17.663
We read the public evidence packet

00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:19.881
and verified its fingerprint.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.302
OntoGraph binds three fields to one
rule:

00:00:25.302 --> 00:00:29.944
the change identifier, its source
link, and its authority.

00:00:29.944 --> 00:00:32.322
Publication requires a reviewer vote.

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:34.830
A delivery receipt alone proves
little.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.455
Change the identifier.

00:00:37.455 --> 00:00:42.843
The format still passes, but the rule
puts the signal on hold.

00:00:42.843 --> 00:00:44.528
Edit just the summary,

00:00:44.528 --> 00:00:47.830
and the full signal fingerprint
catches that too.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.402
The original signal reached PALO.

00:00:51.402 --> 00:00:55.511
Its local client reopened Measure and
Prove.

00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:58.272
The case is waiting for a human.

00:00:58.272 --> 00:01:00.714
Nobody approved a production change.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.987
Now try OntoGraph on its own.

00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:07.725
A calibration lab ran offline with its
own dictionary.

00:01:07.725 --> 00:01:10.196
Its complete certificate passed.

00:01:10.196 --> 00:01:14.830
Missing data put another on hold. A
draft was outside scope.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.668
The lab withdrew the release.

00:01:17.668 --> 00:01:20.437
Its receipt left the outcome open.

00:01:20.437 --> 00:01:23.268
Only an observation that the rule had
stopped running

00:01:23.268 --> 00:01:24.830
confirmed withdrawal.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.337
Which piece of evidence would you
trust?

00:01:28.337 --> 00:01:29.549
Try the case.
